# 🎓 Student Enrollment & Course Management System (SECMS)

A Salesforce-based Student Enrollment & Course Management System designed to manage **Students, Courses, Instructors, Enrollments, Approvals, Automation, Security, Reports, and Dashboards** in a centralized Lightning App.

**Platform:** Salesforce
**Project Type:** Salesforce Administrator Hands-on Project
**Program:** SmartBridge
**Progress:** 90%

---

## 📌 Project Overview

The **Student Enrollment & Course Management System (SECMS)** is designed to digitalize the complete student enrollment lifecycle.

Before implementing Salesforce, student and enrollment information was managed through spreadsheets and emails. SECMS centralizes this information using **Custom Objects, Relationships, Validation Rules, Approval Processes, Flows, Security, Reports, and Dashboards**.

The system provides a structured and efficient way to manage student enrollment and course-related information within a single Salesforce Lightning App.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

* Create a custom data model for Students, Courses, Enrollments, and Instructors.
* Automate enrollment date population.
* Automate approval notifications through email.
* Enforce business rules using Validation Rules.
* Manage enrollment requests through an Approval Process.
* Provide role-based security and access control.
* Create reports and dashboards for real-time monitoring.
* Centralize student and course management in a Lightning App.

---

# 🏗️ Phase 2: Backend Development & Configurations

### 1. Custom Objects

| Custom Object   | Purpose                                         |
| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| `Student__c`    | Stores student personal and academic details    |
| `Course__c`     | Stores the course catalog                       |
| `Enrollment__c` | Junction object connecting Students and Courses |
| `Instructor__c` | Stores instructor details                       |

---

### 2. Student Object Fields

The Student object contains fields based on the requirements of the system.

**Data Types Used:**

* Text
* Email
* Picklist
* Date
* Lookup

**Purpose:**
To ensure accurate student information storage and proper mapping of business requirements.

---

### 3. Relationships

The system uses Salesforce relationships to connect students, courses, and enrollments.

* **Lookup Relationship:** Student → Enrollment
* **Junction Object:** `Enrollment__c`
* **Relationship Type:** Many-to-Many between Students and Courses

**Benefit:**
Provides proper data linking, consistency, and data integrity.

---

### 4. Validation Rules

Validation Rules are implemented to prevent invalid data entry.

**Example: Student Email Domain Validation**

The validation rule ensures that students enter valid email domains according to the defined business requirement.

**Purpose:**

* Prevent invalid data.
* Improve data accuracy.
* Enforce business rules.

---

### 5. Approval Process

### Enrollment Requests Approval

The Enrollment Approval Process manages enrollment requests through a defined approval workflow.

**Approval Flow:**

```text
Submitted
    ↓
Department Head Review
    ↓
Approved / Rejected
    ↓
Automatic Email Notification
```

This provides a structured process for reviewing and managing enrollment requests.

---

# 🎨 Phase 3: UI/UX Development & Customization

## Lightning App

A centralized **Student Management App** is created to provide easy access to the major objects and features.

### Tabs

Tabs are created for easy navigation and management of:

* Students
* Courses
* Enrollments
* Instructors

---

## Page Layouts & Record Types

Page Layouts and Record Types are configured to control the fields and information displayed to users.

### Enrollment Record Types

Different layouts are configured for:

* Full-time
* Part-time

**Benefits:**

* Displays only relevant fields.
* Reduces unnecessary data entry.
* Improves user experience.
* Supports different enrollment scenarios.

---

# ⚙️ Phase 4: Data Migration, Testing & Security

## Automation with Flow

### Auto-Populate Enrollment Date

A **Record-Triggered Flow** is used to automatically populate the enrollment date when an enrollment record is created.

### Approval Email Notification

An **Email Alert** is configured to send notifications when an enrollment request is approved.

---

# 📊 Reports

The system includes reports for monitoring important student and enrollment information.

### Available Reports

* **Students by Status**
* **Enrollments by Course**
* **Pending Enrollment Approvals**

These reports provide useful information for monitoring and decision-making.

---

# 📈 Dashboard

## Student Management Dashboard

The Student Management Dashboard provides a real-time overview of student enrollment information.

It helps users monitor enrollment-related information through Salesforce dashboard components.

---

# 🔐 Security Setup

SECMS uses Salesforce security features to control access to system information.

### Profiles & Permission Sets

Role-based access is configured using:

* Profiles
* Permission Sets

### Field-Level Security

Field-Level Security is used to protect confidential information and control which fields users can access.

---

# 📁 Project Structure

```text
force-app/
└── main/
    └── default/
        ├── objects/
        │   ├── Student__c/
        │   ├── Course__c/
        │   ├── Enrollment__c/
        │   └── Instructor__c/
        │
        ├── tabs/
        ├── flexipages/
        ├── flows/
        ├── approvalProcesses/
        └── validationRules/
```

